1
00:00:58,525 --> 00:01:01,070
Previously on Dating Alys Perez.

2
00:01:02,362 --> 00:01:03,530
What did you do?!

3
00:01:04,073 --> 00:01:05,783
Fier is pregnant!

4
00:01:06,418 --> 00:01:08,378
You can't be with Alys!

5
00:01:12,956 --> 00:01:14,374
Alys...

6
00:01:14,833 --> 00:01:16,543
Just go, Drake. Leave me alone!

7
00:01:16,543 --> 00:01:17,711
Alys, wait!

8
00:01:17,711 --> 00:01:18,962
- I said, leave!
- Alys!

9
00:01:18,962 --> 00:01:21,965
- Can't you understand?
- Alys, I love you, not Fier.

10
00:01:22,841 --> 00:01:24,802
You freaking banged me

11
00:01:24,802 --> 00:01:27,346
and you’re telling me
you don’t want to take responsibility?

12
00:01:27,346 --> 00:01:28,847
Fier, I won’t run away from you.

13
00:01:29,011 --> 00:01:31,430
Drake Sebastian Jimenez Palma...

14
00:01:32,218 --> 00:01:34,858
Will you please marry this selfish girl?

15
00:02:01,463 --> 00:02:02,965
Mom, Dad,

16
00:02:03,632 --> 00:02:05,259
I have something to say.

17
00:02:07,601 --> 00:02:08,936
Drake and I...

18
00:02:13,151 --> 00:02:14,486
We're getting married.

19
00:02:20,779 --> 00:02:22,572
I'm sorry, Alys. But you can't.

20
00:02:30,367 --> 00:02:31,451
Alys,

21
00:02:32,119 --> 00:02:33,078
you can't marry him.

22
00:02:33,328 --> 00:02:35,706
But why, Dad? Give me a reason!

23
00:02:35,731 --> 00:02:36,732
Alys!

24
00:02:36,831 --> 00:02:38,041
Don't shout at your Dad.

25
00:02:38,632 --> 00:02:40,718
How can I not shout at him?! I’m —

26
00:02:41,435 --> 00:02:42,383
Alys.

27
00:02:42,504 --> 00:02:43,630
Calm down.

28
00:02:43,655 --> 00:02:45,115
How can I calm down?

29
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:47,392
Why can't we get married?

30
00:02:47,417 --> 00:02:49,628
Because Drake is having a
baby with someone else!

31
00:02:50,168 --> 00:02:51,938
What in that sentence
can't you understand?

32
00:02:52,222 --> 00:02:53,157
Auntie...

33
00:02:53,269 --> 00:02:54,324
Drake,

34
00:02:54,349 --> 00:02:55,392
you just can't.

35
00:02:58,611 --> 00:02:59,862
Oh, come on, Mom!

36
00:02:59,887 --> 00:03:01,430
Don't be such a freakin' hypocrite!

37
00:03:01,603 --> 00:03:04,064
Dad accepted you even when
you had a child that wasn’t his.

38
00:03:04,119 --> 00:03:05,078
Why can’t —

39
00:03:07,177 --> 00:03:08,470
Alys,

40
00:03:08,495 --> 00:03:10,080
I'm sorry.

41
00:03:25,026 --> 00:03:26,152
Drake.

42
00:03:32,789 --> 00:03:34,707
Do you really love my daughter?

43
00:03:37,697 --> 00:03:39,031
Yes, Uncle.

44
00:03:39,686 --> 00:03:42,231
That’s the only thing I’m certain
about in my life right now.

45
00:03:43,541 --> 00:03:44,824
And...

46
00:03:45,428 --> 00:03:48,097
what happened between
you and the girl?

47
00:03:51,487 --> 00:03:53,322
Alys, please.

48
00:03:53,538 --> 00:03:54,372
Please!

49
00:03:54,397 --> 00:03:56,191
I can't do this right now, Mom.

50
00:03:56,552 --> 00:03:58,136
I’m not in the right headspace.

51
00:03:59,049 --> 00:04:00,342
What are you doing, Alys?

52
00:04:00,389 --> 00:04:02,516
It’s all just too painful for me.

53
00:04:02,541 --> 00:04:05,586
It hurts my brain,
my heart and my soul!

54
00:04:05,611 --> 00:04:08,048
I feel like I'm being beaten up!

55
00:04:08,048 --> 00:04:09,777
Alys, please.

56
00:04:09,802 --> 00:04:10,970
I didn't want to break down,

57
00:04:11,009 --> 00:04:13,347
but things just pushed me to.

58
00:04:13,372 --> 00:04:14,415
What are you doing, Alys?

59
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:15,524
I'm running away!

60
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:19,269
Are you sure?

61
00:04:19,294 --> 00:04:20,796
It was just one time?

62
00:04:23,343 --> 00:04:24,845
That was...

63
00:04:27,650 --> 00:04:30,361
That was lapse of
judgment on my part, Uncle.

64
00:04:31,642 --> 00:04:33,777
Alys and I had
broken up at that time.

65
00:04:34,116 --> 00:04:36,410
I thought we’d never
get back together.

66
00:04:36,785 --> 00:04:39,705
But then I realized, that Alys
was the only one for me.

67
00:04:39,967 --> 00:04:42,303
And if it’s not her,
then I’d rather be alone.

68
00:04:44,835 --> 00:04:46,332
I really,

69
00:04:46,797 --> 00:04:48,924
really love your daughter, Uncle.

70
00:04:50,050 --> 00:04:52,219
She’s the only one I’ve ever loved,

71
00:04:52,329 --> 00:04:53,902
and the only one I ever will.

72
00:04:57,727 --> 00:04:59,729
Just make sure you sort things out.

73
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:02,886
It may be hard now.

74
00:05:03,202 --> 00:05:05,412
But eventually,
everything will be okay.

75
00:05:06,429 --> 00:05:07,754
I hope so, Uncle.

76
00:05:10,235 --> 00:05:11,111
Alys.

77
00:05:11,111 --> 00:05:12,029
Drake!

78
00:05:12,029 --> 00:05:13,613
Are you leaving Mommy?

79
00:05:15,365 --> 00:05:16,116
Go.

80
00:05:16,992 --> 00:05:18,368
Thank you.

81
00:05:22,234 --> 00:05:23,694
- Alys.
- Drake!

82
00:05:23,719 --> 00:05:25,888
Come on, let's go!

83
00:05:31,298 --> 00:05:33,800
Drake, let's go.
We're running away.

84
00:05:44,785 --> 00:05:47,037
You don't wanna run
away with me, don't you?

85
00:05:50,609 --> 00:05:51,636
Alys,

86
00:05:52,336 --> 00:05:54,505
running away is not a solution.

87
00:06:03,497 --> 00:06:06,833
If you’re not going to be with
me through this, then leave.

88
00:06:13,730 --> 00:06:16,066
Alys, Alys!

89
00:06:17,249 --> 00:06:18,208
Leave, Drake!

90
00:06:18,233 --> 00:06:19,318
Leave me alone, Drake!

91
00:06:19,513 --> 00:06:20,680
Just go!

92
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,974
Leave, Drake! Leave!

93
00:06:22,974 --> 00:06:25,268
Leave! I said, leave!

94
00:06:25,268 --> 00:06:27,145
I said, leave!

95
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:30,118
Leave me alone!

96
00:09:22,302 --> 00:09:23,380
Tripp...

97
00:09:24,110 --> 00:09:25,278
Alys?

98
00:09:25,870 --> 00:09:27,288
Are you crying again?

99
00:09:28,055 --> 00:09:28,931
Where are you?

100
00:09:30,453 --> 00:09:31,579
Where are you?

101
00:09:31,604 --> 00:09:33,272
Can I please go there?

102
00:09:34,491 --> 00:09:35,451
Please?

103
00:09:37,442 --> 00:09:39,611
You shouldn’t leave in that state, Zy.

104
00:09:41,021 --> 00:09:42,230
I'll go to you.

105
00:09:42,645 --> 00:09:43,938
Where are you?

106
00:09:44,384 --> 00:09:45,427
No.

107
00:09:45,427 --> 00:09:48,054
No, Tripp listen to me.

108
00:09:49,514 --> 00:09:50,807
I can't.

109
00:09:50,807 --> 00:09:52,934
I can't stay here any longer.

110
00:09:53,243 --> 00:09:54,161
I feel like...

111
00:09:54,186 --> 00:09:57,814
I feel like my sanity would
just fly out of the window.

112
00:09:57,839 --> 00:10:00,800
I can't stay here any longer.

113
00:10:01,693 --> 00:10:03,364
Please, Tripp...

114
00:10:03,596 --> 00:10:05,431
Please!

115
00:10:05,456 --> 00:10:07,082
Can I just go there?

116
00:10:07,107 --> 00:10:08,609
Please help me.

117
00:10:09,159 --> 00:10:10,216
Okay.

118
00:10:10,479 --> 00:10:11,605
Okay.

119
00:10:11,630 --> 00:10:12,756
I hear you.

120
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:14,930
I'll just send you the address.

121
00:10:14,955 --> 00:10:15,997
And I'll pick you up.

122
00:10:16,022 --> 00:10:17,028
Okay?

123
00:10:19,706 --> 00:10:21,291
Thank you, Tripp.

124
00:10:21,853 --> 00:10:23,146
Okay.

125
00:10:25,216 --> 00:10:26,509
Ugh, seriously.

126
00:10:42,901 --> 00:10:45,153
Unbelievable.

127
00:10:50,742 --> 00:10:52,226
I never learn.

128
00:11:00,303 --> 00:11:01,632
It’s still about him.

129
00:11:12,413 --> 00:11:13,706
You love him, right?

130
00:11:14,270 --> 00:11:17,690
So much.

131
00:11:17,894 --> 00:11:19,521
Too much.

132
00:11:20,342 --> 00:11:22,135
Giving up is hard, Zy.

133
00:11:23,936 --> 00:11:25,270
So hard.

134
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:29,454
Especially me, I know.

135
00:11:31,093 --> 00:11:32,553
If I hadn't given up,

136
00:11:34,598 --> 00:11:35,969
you'd be with me instead.

137
00:11:41,501 --> 00:11:43,336
You know what, Zy?

138
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:45,178
Honestly,

139
00:11:45,695 --> 00:11:48,906
I don't know what I can
do to make you feel better.

140
00:11:52,055 --> 00:11:53,932
Tripp, it really hurts.

141
00:11:59,159 --> 00:12:00,160
Come here.

142
00:12:00,185 --> 00:12:02,395
Maybe we’d be happy
and at peace right now,

143
00:12:02,420 --> 00:12:04,589
if he were the one I loved so deeply.

144
00:12:04,614 --> 00:12:06,658
I just know that he wouldn't hurt me.

145
00:12:06,683 --> 00:12:07,934
You know, Zy.

146
00:12:10,996 --> 00:12:12,414
He would hurt you,

147
00:12:16,353 --> 00:12:17,563
but it'll be worth it.

148
00:12:18,467 --> 00:12:19,677
That's how it goes, Zy.

149
00:12:22,505 --> 00:12:24,048
When it comes to the person you love,

150
00:12:25,583 --> 00:12:27,752
no matter how painful,

151
00:12:28,882 --> 00:12:30,508
no matter how long it takes,

152
00:12:33,511 --> 00:12:35,138
it'll all be worth it in the end.

153
00:12:39,031 --> 00:12:40,282
Here.

154
00:12:41,645 --> 00:12:42,687
Come on.

155
00:12:43,018 --> 00:12:44,144
Go eat.

156
00:12:44,663 --> 00:12:45,705
Your fries,

157
00:12:46,603 --> 00:12:47,896
and your burger.

158
00:12:49,621 --> 00:12:50,914
Thank you.

159
00:13:00,622 --> 00:13:01,696
You know,

160
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:05,786
you've always been like this.

161
00:13:06,281 --> 00:13:08,241
I need to remind you before you eat.

162
00:13:10,391 --> 00:13:12,435
You’re so harsh with me.

163
00:13:12,802 --> 00:13:15,221
I do eat on my own sometimes.

164
00:13:22,818 --> 00:13:24,069
Remember Brenford?

165
00:13:25,842 --> 00:13:28,303
The park where we used to hang out?

166
00:13:30,902 --> 00:13:32,278
Yes.

167
00:13:33,583 --> 00:13:35,626
You always had your camera with you.

168
00:13:36,845 --> 00:13:38,555
What happened to that?

169
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:41,886
Well...

170
00:13:43,393 --> 00:13:46,897
my dreams were swept away,
the moment I entered the real world.

171
00:13:49,170 --> 00:13:52,215
Happens to everyone, doesn't it?

172
00:13:54,217 --> 00:13:58,429
Dreams change as we grow older.

173
00:13:59,138 --> 00:14:01,516
Replaced by new ones.

174
00:14:06,771 --> 00:14:09,023
But there’s one dream
that never changed.

175
00:14:10,316 --> 00:14:11,526
What?

176
00:14:14,445 --> 00:14:16,155
I think the question should be...

177
00:14:16,781 --> 00:14:17,740
who?

178
00:14:25,456 --> 00:14:26,833
Tripp.

179
00:14:26,833 --> 00:14:27,709
Hmm?

180
00:14:28,918 --> 00:14:30,587
If I ask you

181
00:14:30,587 --> 00:14:32,380
to run away with me,

182
00:14:33,362 --> 00:14:34,530
would you?

183
00:14:39,105 --> 00:14:40,106
You know what,

184
00:14:40,131 --> 00:14:41,674
just finish your dinner, Zy.

185
00:14:42,608 --> 00:14:44,527
You’re thinking of all sorts of things.

186
00:14:44,552 --> 00:14:45,303
Look,

187
00:14:45,328 --> 00:14:47,580
you haven't touched it the
whole time we were here.

188
00:14:47,936 --> 00:14:49,188
Are you eating like a bird?

189
00:14:54,027 --> 00:14:55,278
Eat first.

190
00:14:56,279 --> 00:14:57,530
Then I'll take you home.

191
00:14:59,866 --> 00:15:01,159
But I don't wanna go home.

192
00:15:01,159 --> 00:15:03,578
I told you, I don't wanna be there.

193
00:15:03,911 --> 00:15:05,329
Please, Tripp.

194
00:15:05,455 --> 00:15:07,332
I don't wanna go home.

195
00:15:10,452 --> 00:15:11,870
- Tripp!
- Zy.

196
00:15:12,003 --> 00:15:13,546
- Zy...
- Please?

197
00:15:14,623 --> 00:15:17,278
Running away won't do anything good.

198
00:15:19,260 --> 00:15:20,528
Trust me.

199
00:15:26,267 --> 00:15:28,353
It hurts knowing you're choosing me again.

200
00:15:29,646 --> 00:15:31,731
Not because you truly want me,

201
00:15:32,315 --> 00:15:34,876
but because things between you
and Drake aren't working out.

202
00:15:35,526 --> 00:15:36,642
Again.

203
00:16:14,649 --> 00:16:17,906
My body’s exhausted,
but my mind is wide awake.

204
00:16:19,237 --> 00:16:20,863
It wouldn't let me sleep.

205
00:16:21,464 --> 00:16:22,937
And the worst part is,

206
00:16:23,241 --> 00:16:24,409
it’s even harder to think when

207
00:16:24,409 --> 00:16:27,046
your mind is filled
with painful thoughts.

208
00:16:29,257 --> 00:16:31,968
Good thing I don't
have any plans today.

209
00:16:33,008 --> 00:16:35,757
I mean, I have work but...

210
00:16:37,122 --> 00:16:38,843
I don’t want to deal with it yet.

211
00:16:41,634 --> 00:16:45,585
I just want to run, escape and breathe.

212
00:16:46,973 --> 00:16:48,182
Whatever.

213
00:16:55,470 --> 00:16:56,679
Alys.

214
00:17:02,071 --> 00:17:03,281
I'm sorry.

215
00:17:03,740 --> 00:17:04,949
Okay.

216
00:17:10,751 --> 00:17:11,752
Are you mad at me?

217
00:17:14,249 --> 00:17:15,085
No.

218
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:20,173
Where were you last night?

219
00:17:21,321 --> 00:17:22,322
With Tripp.

220
00:17:28,514 --> 00:17:31,267
I almost asked him to
run away with me, you know.

221
00:17:34,812 --> 00:17:35,938
But you didn't.

222
00:17:41,569 --> 00:17:42,737
Yeah, I didn't.

223
00:17:44,572 --> 00:17:46,783
I promised you I
wouldn't leave you, right?

224
00:17:48,544 --> 00:17:50,546
Just marry me already, Drake.

225
00:17:51,068 --> 00:17:52,736
I’m losing my mind here.

226
00:17:52,761 --> 00:17:53,762
I’m about to snap.

227
00:17:58,142 --> 00:17:59,435
Yes, Alys.

228
00:18:00,365 --> 00:18:01,992
I will marry you.

229
00:18:02,792 --> 00:18:04,336
Thank you.

230
00:18:11,314 --> 00:18:12,899
Let them be angry.

231
00:18:13,370 --> 00:18:15,414
Even your mom and dad.

232
00:18:16,037 --> 00:18:17,075
But yes.

233
00:18:17,803 --> 00:18:19,013
We will get married.

234
00:18:21,783 --> 00:18:24,953
Is this the start of
our happily ever after?

235
00:18:24,978 --> 00:18:26,021
I hope so.

236
00:18:26,572 --> 00:18:27,698
Alys...

237
00:18:27,944 --> 00:18:28,802
Zyril...

238
00:18:29,069 --> 00:18:30,013
Perez.

239
00:18:31,327 --> 00:18:32,130
Hmm?

240
00:18:33,950 --> 00:18:35,076
Will you marry me?

241
00:18:41,254 --> 00:18:42,338
Yes.

242
00:18:48,471 --> 00:18:49,806
Love is patient.

243
00:18:50,520 --> 00:18:51,855
Love is kind.

244
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:53,214
Drake Palma!

245
00:18:53,985 --> 00:18:56,570
You're my boyfriend now!

246
00:18:57,999 --> 00:18:59,167
It does not envy.

247
00:19:00,214 --> 00:19:01,465
It does not boast.

248
00:19:01,490 --> 00:19:02,575
I'm Alys.

249
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:04,226
Alys Zyril Perez.

250
00:19:04,251 --> 00:19:05,878
Soon to be Palma.

251
00:19:05,903 --> 00:19:07,113
Hello!

252
00:19:07,618 --> 00:19:08,941
It is not proud.

253
00:19:10,005 --> 00:19:11,673
It is not self-seeking.

254
00:19:12,690 --> 00:19:14,358
It is not easily angered.

255
00:19:15,413 --> 00:19:17,290
It keeps no record of wrongs.

256
00:19:18,295 --> 00:19:20,172
Love does not delight in evil.

257
00:19:21,108 --> 00:19:22,985
But rejoices with the truth.

258
00:19:23,519 --> 00:19:24,556
I'm territorial.

259
00:19:25,313 --> 00:19:26,481
I'm territorial.

260
00:19:26,819 --> 00:19:28,195
I'm territorial.

261
00:19:28,555 --> 00:19:29,932
It always protects.

262
00:19:30,910 --> 00:19:32,286
It always trusts.

263
00:19:33,377 --> 00:19:34,754
It always hopes.

264
00:19:35,132 --> 00:19:37,176
It always perseveres.

265
00:19:39,710 --> 00:19:42,004
Love never fails.

266
00:19:43,721 --> 00:19:46,015
And by the authority vested in me

267
00:19:46,040 --> 00:19:50,461
by Article 7, Paragraph 1 of the
Family Code of the Philippines.

268
00:19:50,598 --> 00:19:53,392
Calling all those present
here as witnesses,

269
00:19:53,417 --> 00:19:56,087
Patrick Sanchez and Gail Cortez.

270
00:19:56,112 --> 00:19:58,030
I now pronounce you

271
00:19:58,830 --> 00:19:59,728
man and wife.

272
00:19:59,768 --> 00:20:01,520
You may now kiss the bride.

273
00:20:11,505 --> 00:20:13,382
Hey, take it easy.

274
00:20:14,147 --> 00:20:15,523
It's not your honeymoon yet.

275
00:20:15,548 --> 00:20:16,924
I’m sorry.

276
00:20:19,567 --> 00:20:21,111
- Thank you, bro.
- Congratulations.

277
00:20:21,136 --> 00:20:23,346
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

278
00:20:34,793 --> 00:20:35,564
What?

279
00:20:37,445 --> 00:20:38,488
Nothing.

280
00:20:38,513 --> 00:20:41,141
I just can't believe we're finally married!

281
00:20:42,234 --> 00:20:44,111
For heaven's sake!

282
00:20:44,545 --> 00:20:46,255
Are you happy, Alys?

283
00:20:46,966 --> 00:20:50,136
Words can't suffice how
I'm feeling right now.

284
00:20:51,275 --> 00:20:52,318
But yes,

285
00:20:52,442 --> 00:20:55,278
I'm very, very much happy.

286
00:20:56,055 --> 00:20:57,473
Good to know.

287
00:20:57,473 --> 00:20:59,892
Because I'm very happy, too.

288
00:21:00,351 --> 00:21:02,645
Even if it's not your dream wedding, Alys.

289
00:21:02,645 --> 00:21:06,524
I promise you, I'll give you
that dream wedding soon.

290
00:21:07,649 --> 00:21:09,860
Oh, come on.
Even if it's just a civil wedding,

291
00:21:10,079 --> 00:21:11,121
we're still married.

292
00:21:11,146 --> 00:21:13,150
And that's what's important.

293
00:21:15,642 --> 00:21:17,686
So, where are we going?

294
00:21:18,183 --> 00:21:19,434
To forever.

295
00:21:24,471 --> 00:21:28,225
This might be the happiest day of my life.

296
00:21:36,850 --> 00:21:38,704
Drake, why are we here?

297
00:21:52,486 --> 00:21:54,196
Drake, what are we doing here?

298
00:21:58,711 --> 00:22:01,630
Drake, seriously, why are we here?

299
00:22:06,369 --> 00:22:07,745
I’ll introduce you to them.

300
00:22:12,114 --> 00:22:16,702
Your family already knows me,
Drake Sebastian Palma.

301
00:22:17,266 --> 00:22:20,894
They know you as Alys – my girlfriend,

302
00:22:21,411 --> 00:22:23,746
as Alys – my heartbreaker,

303
00:22:23,771 --> 00:22:26,941
as Alys – I've been
chasing for all these years.

304
00:22:30,068 --> 00:22:31,569
So what do you mean?

305
00:22:31,859 --> 00:22:33,736
I'm introducing you

306
00:22:34,358 --> 00:22:36,525
as Alys Zyril

307
00:22:36,989 --> 00:22:37,907
Palma.

308
00:22:38,515 --> 00:22:39,767
My wife.

309
00:22:41,744 --> 00:22:42,870
Ready?

310
00:22:49,418 --> 00:22:50,544
But,

311
00:22:54,130 --> 00:22:55,423
I'm nervous.

312
00:22:56,471 --> 00:22:57,532
Me too.

313
00:23:04,179 --> 00:23:05,306
We can do this.

314
00:23:07,603 --> 00:23:09,272
Come on, we've been through worse.

315
00:23:09,912 --> 00:23:11,455
I'm sure we can get through this.

316
00:23:12,619 --> 00:23:13,556
Let's go?

317
00:23:17,806 --> 00:23:18,974
Let's go, Drake.

318
00:23:21,027 --> 00:23:21,829
Wait.

319
00:23:28,412 --> 00:23:30,642
OMG, is this for real?

320
00:23:53,315 --> 00:23:54,400
Let’s go.

321
00:23:59,148 --> 00:24:01,150
Answer me, Alys!

322
00:24:02,825 --> 00:24:05,119
Why is she not picking up?

323
00:24:08,558 --> 00:24:11,353
I wonder if Alys’s message is true.

324
00:24:12,232 --> 00:24:13,942
Or was it a prank?

325
00:24:15,615 --> 00:24:18,118
Why would she even marry Drake?

326
00:24:18,143 --> 00:24:19,227
Is she insane?

327
00:24:20,044 --> 00:24:21,963
- Who got married?
- Oh god.

328
00:24:23,408 --> 00:24:25,077
Oh, Auntie...

329
00:24:25,102 --> 00:24:26,019
our client!

330
00:24:26,044 --> 00:24:29,548
M-miss... Alonzo!

331
00:24:29,602 --> 00:24:32,313
- Okay, and what about her?
- She got married.

332
00:24:32,338 --> 00:24:34,454
She just messaged us,

333
00:24:34,815 --> 00:24:37,048
to say thank you.

334
00:24:37,193 --> 00:24:40,488
Because we did her wedding gown.

335
00:24:40,488 --> 00:24:42,740
Aww, that's so sweet.

336
00:24:42,740 --> 00:24:45,493
Well, tell her thank you
for supporting us, okay?

337
00:24:45,493 --> 00:24:47,786
Yes, Auntie. I'll pass it along.

338
00:24:47,995 --> 00:24:49,038
Alright.

339
00:24:49,387 --> 00:24:50,429
Wow!

340
00:24:50,454 --> 00:24:53,499
That's sweet of Uncle Andy!

341
00:24:53,584 --> 00:24:55,681
A bouquet of flowers!

342
00:24:55,706 --> 00:24:59,543
Oh no, this isn't from him
and this isn't for me!

343
00:24:59,673 --> 00:25:01,165
It's for you.

344
00:25:01,190 --> 00:25:01,858
For me?

345
00:25:01,883 --> 00:25:02,842
Yeah!

346
00:25:05,871 --> 00:25:08,624
Anyway, let me check
the status of your sketch.

347
00:25:08,784 --> 00:25:10,077
Here, Auntie.

348
00:25:10,798 --> 00:25:12,102
Okay.

349
00:25:12,785 --> 00:25:14,371
Alright, I'll be back later, okay?

350
00:25:14,396 --> 00:25:15,356
Thank you!

351
00:25:15,952 --> 00:25:17,203
Thank you.

352
00:25:22,917 --> 00:25:24,043
I still miss you, Bee.

353
00:25:24,254 --> 00:25:25,556
Let’s make up.

354
00:25:26,867 --> 00:25:28,056
Honey?

355
00:25:44,999 --> 00:25:47,752
So what do you want
me to do now, Fier?

356
00:25:51,517 --> 00:25:54,270
Stay here. I'll be back for you.

357
00:26:10,220 --> 00:26:12,180
So, the jerk is here.

358
00:26:13,219 --> 00:26:14,471
You loser! How dare you?!

359
00:26:14,707 --> 00:26:16,375
Dad, Dad!

360
00:26:16,750 --> 00:26:19,587
Dad, I didn't give you his name
so you could start a fight!

361
00:26:19,587 --> 00:26:20,879
I thought we're here to talk.

362
00:26:22,007 --> 00:26:22,962
Shut up, Fier!

363
00:26:23,353 --> 00:26:25,790
I didn't raise you to be
pregnant and unwed!

364
00:26:26,014 --> 00:26:28,100
- But, Dad!
- I said shut up!

365
00:26:28,978 --> 00:26:31,063
And you, Palma...

366
00:26:31,682 --> 00:26:33,642
You better marry my daughter.

367
00:26:34,184 --> 00:26:36,270
If you don’t want to see me get angry.

368
00:26:36,270 --> 00:26:38,897
Mr. Sandoval, please!
We can resolve this calmly.

369
00:26:38,922 --> 00:26:41,133
Let’s fix this. Let's settle this.

370
00:26:42,026 --> 00:26:43,068
Mr. Palma,

371
00:26:43,068 --> 00:26:47,072
as a father I won't let my daughter
be knocked up and derailed like this.

372
00:26:47,156 --> 00:26:48,073
I understand.

373
00:26:48,098 --> 00:26:50,518
What do you want?
How can we resolve this?

374
00:26:50,812 --> 00:26:53,148
I want for your son to marry my daughter.

375
00:26:55,697 --> 00:26:56,548
Drake.

376
00:26:58,382 --> 00:26:59,091
No, Dad.

377
00:26:59,123 --> 00:27:00,875
- What?!
- Dad, stop! Dad.

378
00:27:00,900 --> 00:27:02,860
Stop, stop. Dad, please.

379
00:27:03,672 --> 00:27:04,632
Mr. Sandoval, please.

380
00:27:04,632 --> 00:27:07,509
I can't let you scold my
son inside our own house.

381
00:27:07,509 --> 00:27:09,345
Let's settle this peacefully.

382
00:27:10,371 --> 00:27:11,956
Fine, talk to your son.

383
00:27:13,474 --> 00:27:15,142
Drake, won't you reconsider?

384
00:27:15,476 --> 00:27:16,685
No, Dad.

385
00:27:18,361 --> 00:27:19,612
I refuse.

386
00:27:19,637 --> 00:27:20,930
Not now,

387
00:27:20,955 --> 00:27:22,164
not ever.

388
00:27:22,232 --> 00:27:23,984
- You asshole!
- Dad, Dad, please!

389
00:27:23,984 --> 00:27:26,540
- Dad, please!
- Dad, Dad!

390
00:27:26,565 --> 00:27:27,774
He doesn't love me.

391
00:27:27,944 --> 00:27:30,113
And I also don't wanna push myself.

392
00:27:30,175 --> 00:27:31,885
So please, let's just go home.

393
00:27:31,910 --> 00:27:33,578
She's right, Dad. Don't push it.

394
00:27:33,886 --> 00:27:36,055
Shut up, Lourd!
I’m not talking to you!

395
00:27:36,205 --> 00:27:37,373
Don't interfere.

396
00:27:37,373 --> 00:27:38,791
You're getting married.

397
00:27:38,816 --> 00:27:39,942
And you'll do what I say!

398
00:27:40,841 --> 00:27:43,844
If he won't marry you,
then you're not coming home.

399
00:27:43,869 --> 00:27:45,538
I'll cut all your resources!

400
00:27:45,781 --> 00:27:46,865
You'll have to stay here,

401
00:27:46,890 --> 00:27:48,976
until this jerk marries you!

402
00:27:49,314 --> 00:27:50,290
What?!

403
00:27:50,669 --> 00:27:51,711
Let's go.

404
00:27:52,372 --> 00:27:54,123
Lourd, Chance.

405
00:27:55,239 --> 00:27:57,907
One more thing, Mr. Palma.
The next time we meet,

406
00:27:58,336 --> 00:28:00,130
I hope it will be a pleasant one.

407
00:28:01,050 --> 00:28:03,636
Dad, wait. Don't leave me here!

408
00:28:03,833 --> 00:28:05,168
Dad, wait!

409
00:28:05,423 --> 00:28:07,425
Dad, are you really leaving Fier behind?

410
00:28:07,450 --> 00:28:09,577
Yes, it's her fault for getting knocked up.

411
00:28:11,532 --> 00:28:12,700
But Dad...

412
00:28:13,606 --> 00:28:15,691
The two of you, get it together.

413
00:28:15,762 --> 00:28:18,014
You don't want to see me get angry, too.

414
00:28:18,882 --> 00:28:21,093
As for me, I'm always protected.

415
00:28:21,283 --> 00:28:22,158
Asshole!

416
00:28:22,183 --> 00:28:23,684
What? I didn't do anything.

417
00:28:24,112 --> 00:28:26,531
Both of you shut up. Let's go.

418
00:28:26,952 --> 00:28:28,871
I'll leave you two alone to talk.

419
00:28:40,880 --> 00:28:42,882
Should I go up to Drake?

420
00:28:43,646 --> 00:28:44,981
What do I do?

421
00:28:45,419 --> 00:28:48,756
I thought I've been through the worst.

422
00:28:49,256 --> 00:28:52,509
I didn't know things
could get even worse.

423
00:28:54,867 --> 00:28:55,876
Drake,

424
00:28:56,370 --> 00:28:57,871
you can't push me away.

425
00:28:58,036 --> 00:28:59,538
I'm pregnant.

426
00:29:00,494 --> 00:29:02,287
I don't want to live on the street.

427
00:29:03,333 --> 00:29:04,126
Fine.

428
00:29:04,626 --> 00:29:05,907
Thank you.

429
00:29:06,795 --> 00:29:08,275
But I won't marry you, Fier.

430
00:29:09,481 --> 00:29:10,608
I know.

431
00:29:10,827 --> 00:29:12,787
But don't plan for the ending yet.

432
00:29:13,879 --> 00:29:15,892
We'll be living under one roof.

433
00:29:16,654 --> 00:29:18,306
You have no idea what could happen.

434
00:29:21,675 --> 00:29:23,009
I'm married, Fier.

435
00:29:25,389 --> 00:29:27,433
I married Alys earlier.

436
00:29:33,597 --> 00:29:35,307
You asshole!

437
00:29:39,912 --> 00:29:40,913
You're crazy.

438
00:29:41,301 --> 00:29:42,427
Crazy in love.

439
00:29:42,623 --> 00:29:44,041
Even before.

440
00:30:07,231 --> 00:30:08,448
I heard everything.

441
00:30:11,151 --> 00:30:12,854
Don't worry, Alys.

442
00:30:14,284 --> 00:30:15,869
I'll take care of everything.

443
00:30:16,706 --> 00:30:17,995
But for now,

444
00:30:18,653 --> 00:30:20,025
the fact remains,

445
00:30:20,878 --> 00:30:23,631
we’re married and there’s nothing
they can do about it anymore.

446
00:30:26,051 --> 00:30:27,135
So what's the plan?

447
00:30:27,839 --> 00:30:29,466
I thought you heard everything?

448
00:30:31,488 --> 00:30:32,823
No, I mean...

449
00:30:33,819 --> 00:30:35,120
What do I do now?

450
00:30:37,625 --> 00:30:39,294
So much has happened today.

451
00:30:40,195 --> 00:30:42,656
We got married without my family knowing.

452
00:30:43,040 --> 00:30:46,376
I can't just go back home and
pretend like nothing happened.

453
00:30:47,354 --> 00:30:50,691
You know that my family's
against our wedding.

454
00:30:54,653 --> 00:30:55,737
Live with me.

455
00:30:56,071 --> 00:30:57,155
What?

456
00:30:58,156 --> 00:30:59,241
Alys,

457
00:31:00,158 --> 00:31:01,952
I said live with me.

458
00:31:05,566 --> 00:31:07,235
We're married.

459
00:31:07,260 --> 00:31:09,262
And I want us to be together.

460
00:31:11,769 --> 00:31:13,228
What about Fier?

461
00:31:14,208 --> 00:31:15,668
She'll have nowhere to stay.

462
00:31:16,269 --> 00:31:17,896
Her father disowned her.

463
00:31:19,386 --> 00:31:20,888
She can stay here.

464
00:31:22,222 --> 00:31:24,558
She just needs a place for now.

465
00:31:26,685 --> 00:31:28,395
So...

466
00:31:29,104 --> 00:31:31,481
we'll both live under one roof?

467
00:31:32,357 --> 00:31:34,735
All three of us?

468
00:31:35,819 --> 00:31:37,195
Physically, yes.

469
00:31:37,946 --> 00:31:39,197
But, emotionally?

470
00:31:40,352 --> 00:31:41,854
It'll just be the two of us.

471
00:31:47,664 --> 00:31:48,916
I don't know, Drake.

472
00:31:50,062 --> 00:31:53,107
Actually, I don't know if
anything's right about this.

473
00:31:54,212 --> 00:31:55,899
Neither do I, Alys.

474
00:31:58,508 --> 00:32:00,636
All I know is I love you so much.

475
00:32:03,472 --> 00:32:04,914
We're married now.

476
00:32:05,726 --> 00:32:07,936
But I have a responsibility to Fier.

477
00:32:09,820 --> 00:32:11,739
And this is the only thing

478
00:32:12,264 --> 00:32:13,557
that I could think of

479
00:32:14,608 --> 00:32:16,109
for the both of you.

480
00:32:30,290 --> 00:32:32,209
This is unfair to Alys.

481
00:32:32,751 --> 00:32:35,170
But this is also unfair to Fier.

482
00:32:35,709 --> 00:32:37,043
But what can I do?

483
00:32:37,808 --> 00:32:39,601
There's no other option.

484
00:32:40,331 --> 00:32:42,125
I can't abandon my wife.

485
00:32:42,729 --> 00:32:45,106
But I have to do right by my child.

486
00:32:46,055 --> 00:32:47,390
When will this end?

487
00:32:47,880 --> 00:32:49,339
This chaos.

488
00:32:53,626 --> 00:32:57,087
So, after this wedding,
what's next?

489
00:32:57,619 --> 00:33:00,413
What about Fier?
What about the baby?

490
00:33:01,196 --> 00:33:03,407
What else will I have to face with Drake?

491
00:33:04,449 --> 00:33:07,553
When will our trials end?

492
00:33:08,124 --> 00:33:10,732
Until when will destiny keep testing us?

493
00:33:13,849 --> 00:33:16,351
I know all is fair in love and war.

494
00:33:16,617 --> 00:33:19,119
When it comes to my cousin,

495
00:33:19,756 --> 00:33:21,967
you're so weak, Alys.

496
00:33:22,579 --> 00:33:24,623
Ouch! That hurts.

497
00:33:25,055 --> 00:33:26,223
Good for you then!

498
00:33:26,392 --> 00:33:29,395
Because you’re an expert
when it comes to love, right?

499
00:33:29,512 --> 00:33:31,514
That’s why you don’t have a girlfriend!

500
00:33:31,641 --> 00:33:32,743
Come on.

501
00:33:32,768 --> 00:33:34,145
Why is this suddenly about me?

502
00:33:34,666 --> 00:33:38,837
What we’re talking about here
is your craziness, Alys.

503
00:33:38,862 --> 00:33:40,655
You should know that.

504
00:33:42,351 --> 00:33:43,248
Listen.

505
00:33:43,785 --> 00:33:45,912
You've been staying at
Drake's for three days

506
00:33:45,937 --> 00:33:47,939
living with that Fier.

507
00:33:48,461 --> 00:33:50,338
Does that sound sane to you?

508
00:33:50,787 --> 00:33:52,914
God, that's peak!

509
00:33:53,232 --> 00:33:55,818
Okay, look. I know the idea was crazy.

510
00:33:56,493 --> 00:33:58,370
But I'm even crazier!

511
00:33:59,224 --> 00:34:02,449
And honestly, never once in my life

512
00:34:02,713 --> 00:34:04,799
did I ever consider doing
something like this.

513
00:34:05,773 --> 00:34:07,400
But I still managed to do it.

514
00:34:08,388 --> 00:34:11,139
- Oh lord!
- So you are self-aware!

515
00:34:13,223 --> 00:34:14,599
And Fier's not even helping.

516
00:34:14,631 --> 00:34:16,425
She's such a bitch, you know!

517
00:34:16,776 --> 00:34:19,195
What?
You expect her to be nice to you?

518
00:34:19,289 --> 00:34:20,568
Hello!

519
00:34:21,345 --> 00:34:22,430
Hello!

520
00:34:23,132 --> 00:34:24,675
That's enough, Tofer!

521
00:34:25,718 --> 00:34:27,636
I can't even sleep at night!

522
00:34:28,076 --> 00:34:30,495
The nights are the most stressful.

523
00:34:30,954 --> 00:34:32,873
I'm about to call the OB.

524
00:34:33,371 --> 00:34:34,915
Fine, I get it.

525
00:34:36,040 --> 00:34:38,668
She's acting like a lunatic
because she's pregnant.

526
00:34:38,731 --> 00:34:40,399
But that doesn't excuse it.

527
00:34:40,424 --> 00:34:43,135
She's pregnant not a psycho.

528
00:34:43,298 --> 00:34:45,092
Fine, Alys.

529
00:34:45,769 --> 00:34:47,020
Let’s talk this through properly.

530
00:34:49,723 --> 00:34:52,088
Alys, what the hell?

531
00:34:52,349 --> 00:34:53,100
What the hell?

532
00:34:53,100 --> 00:34:53,978
Yes!

533
00:34:54,132 --> 00:34:55,842
I know you and Drake are married.

534
00:34:56,480 --> 00:34:58,315
But how did you get yourself

535
00:34:58,933 --> 00:35:01,352
stuck in that house with that —

536
00:35:01,953 --> 00:35:03,163
Excuse me for the term...

537
00:35:03,235 --> 00:35:04,444
Mistress!

538
00:35:06,154 --> 00:35:07,823
Hey, that's too much.

539
00:35:08,365 --> 00:35:11,993
I really don't like it when
people call Fier a mistress.

540
00:35:12,632 --> 00:35:15,426
It hurts. For her and for me.

541
00:35:16,560 --> 00:35:21,231
I mean, it's hard to even force
myself to be angry at her.

542
00:35:22,177 --> 00:35:26,098
I always remember that
she carries Drake's child.

543
00:35:26,216 --> 00:35:29,136
That fact alone is
enough to pacify my heart.

544
00:35:30,597 --> 00:35:33,225
The fact is, that's what she is.

545
00:35:33,824 --> 00:35:36,076
No matter how you look at this,

546
00:35:36,852 --> 00:35:38,770
you're married to Drake.

547
00:35:40,816 --> 00:35:42,109
It hurts to be called a mistress.

548
00:35:44,317 --> 00:35:47,821
And it's not her fault that Drake's
not planning on marrying her.

549
00:35:48,954 --> 00:35:50,873
It's not Drake's fault either.

550
00:35:51,758 --> 00:35:54,386
In fact, it's no one's fault.

551
00:35:55,738 --> 00:35:58,282
We're all just victims of fate.

552
00:35:58,998 --> 00:36:00,791
The timing is just so screwed up.

553
00:36:01,477 --> 00:36:03,312
What do you mean it
wasn't Drake's fault?

554
00:36:03,670 --> 00:36:06,345
He created all of this mess!

555
00:36:07,299 --> 00:36:08,400
Hey, Tofer!

556
00:36:08,830 --> 00:36:11,458
I know you like Tripp over him but

557
00:36:11,553 --> 00:36:13,513
don't take it all out on Drake.

558
00:36:14,725 --> 00:36:15,851
Actually,

559
00:36:16,304 --> 00:36:18,515
he did offer his unit, I just declined.

560
00:36:18,540 --> 00:36:19,783
There it is!

561
00:36:20,520 --> 00:36:22,861
Alys Zyril Perez,

562
00:36:23,381 --> 00:36:26,955
why do you have to
stick yourself in that house

563
00:36:27,139 --> 00:36:29,516
when you have the choice not to?

564
00:36:29,696 --> 00:36:31,642
Why do I want to be there?

565
00:36:31,885 --> 00:36:33,387
I don't know.

566
00:36:33,412 --> 00:36:36,874
Maybe it's because I don't want
Drake to go through this alone.

567
00:36:36,934 --> 00:36:39,895
I don't want him to have to choose.

568
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:42,714
Four years of struggle is enough.

569
00:36:43,960 --> 00:36:45,337
Hey, Tofer,

570
00:36:45,670 --> 00:36:48,715
I came here to relax,
not be scolded by you.

571
00:36:48,795 --> 00:36:51,089
I just came from Aya's sermons,
I don't need yours too.

572
00:36:51,751 --> 00:36:55,421
I asked you to come so I could vent.
Not so you could be my parent.

573
00:36:56,735 --> 00:36:57,987
Annoying.

574
00:36:59,463 --> 00:37:00,714
Fine.

575
00:37:02,580 --> 00:37:05,541
Bestie has gone crazy.

576
00:37:05,925 --> 00:37:08,302
What do I have to do
to get through to her?

577
00:37:11,356 --> 00:37:12,353
S...

578
00:37:17,329 --> 00:37:18,274
O...

579
00:37:21,454 --> 00:37:24,498
R, R...

580
00:37:26,277 --> 00:37:27,237
Y?

581
00:37:27,672 --> 00:37:28,806
Sorry?

582
00:37:30,061 --> 00:37:31,979
Bee! Sorry!

583
00:37:32,315 --> 00:37:33,650
Damn it, Kent.

584
00:37:33,675 --> 00:37:35,218
Did I startle you, Bee?

585
00:37:35,326 --> 00:37:36,536
Isn't it obvious?

586
00:37:36,731 --> 00:37:39,306
Sorry, sorry for everything, Bee.

587
00:37:39,732 --> 00:37:41,368
For startling you,

588
00:37:41,393 --> 00:37:42,769
for being so clingy.

589
00:37:42,769 --> 00:37:44,020
Believe me,

590
00:37:44,267 --> 00:37:45,697
I've learned my lesson!

591
00:37:46,199 --> 00:37:46,838
Geez!

592
00:37:46,905 --> 00:37:48,627
You came just to say sorry?

593
00:37:48,652 --> 00:37:50,237
Is that really all?

594
00:37:50,729 --> 00:37:52,356
You could have just sent a message.

595
00:37:52,997 --> 00:37:54,165
Bee, of course not.

596
00:37:55,122 --> 00:37:56,582
I'm ready to win you back.

597
00:37:59,644 --> 00:38:01,729
Bee, forgive me, please!

598
00:38:01,754 --> 00:38:03,631
Whatever you want, I'll do it.

599
00:38:03,656 --> 00:38:05,575
Let me make it up to you!

600
00:38:05,857 --> 00:38:07,775
We've been apart for so long.

601
00:38:08,004 --> 00:38:09,756
It's driving me insane, Bee!

602
00:38:09,781 --> 00:38:12,325
No, no, get up!
I don't want you to go insane!

603
00:38:12,350 --> 00:38:14,436
It’s enough that I just know
one crazy person.

604
00:38:14,461 --> 00:38:15,939
What? Who?

605
00:38:15,964 --> 00:38:18,967
Whatever, just stand up,
or I won't forgive you!

606
00:38:20,520 --> 00:38:22,730
See? That wasn't hard.

607
00:38:23,059 --> 00:38:24,002
Bee...

608
00:38:24,477 --> 00:38:25,895
Come on, Bee.

609
00:38:26,059 --> 00:38:28,689
I just want us to be back together.

610
00:38:30,512 --> 00:38:33,181
If I forgive this idiot,

611
00:38:33,353 --> 00:38:35,705
does that make me as crazy as Alys?

612
00:38:36,648 --> 00:38:38,233
Probably not.

613
00:38:38,655 --> 00:38:40,115
It's entirely different.

614
00:38:43,754 --> 00:38:45,214
Only if...

615
00:38:46,804 --> 00:38:48,430
you'll court me again.

616
00:38:48,626 --> 00:38:49,794
Huh?

617
00:38:49,794 --> 00:38:51,629
Yeah! Thank you, Bee!

618
00:39:40,178 --> 00:39:41,137
Fier!

619
00:39:41,137 --> 00:39:42,225
Have you eaten yet?

620
00:39:42,331 --> 00:39:43,791
I brought fruits!

621
00:39:46,559 --> 00:39:48,895
What game are we playing here, Alys?

622
00:39:50,062 --> 00:39:50,938
Huh?

623
00:39:52,107 --> 00:39:55,318
Quit acting nice.
I know you're mad at me.

624
00:39:55,648 --> 00:39:58,109
Be bitchy or whatever.
I don't care.

625
00:39:58,435 --> 00:39:59,819
Just quit acting like you care.

626
00:40:00,244 --> 00:40:00,858
Fier...

627
00:40:00,883 --> 00:40:02,301
Drop it, Alys!

628
00:40:04,843 --> 00:40:06,052
You don't care.

629
00:40:06,663 --> 00:40:09,124
Deep inside, you want me
and my child to disappear.

630
00:40:09,124 --> 00:40:10,208
Is that right?

631
00:40:12,293 --> 00:40:13,753
Come on, Fier.

632
00:40:14,998 --> 00:40:16,416
Stop it, Alys.

633
00:40:16,696 --> 00:40:18,865
We both know how this is going to end.

634
00:40:19,860 --> 00:40:21,320
One of us has to go.

635
00:40:22,720 --> 00:40:24,097
You're married to him.

636
00:40:24,764 --> 00:40:26,349
And we're having a child.

637
00:40:26,933 --> 00:40:29,352
Can't you see how crazy our situation is?

638
00:40:32,897 --> 00:40:34,022
This baby?

639
00:40:35,400 --> 00:40:38,403
This baby will be labeled a bastard, Alys.

640
00:40:39,571 --> 00:40:41,030
A bastard!

641
00:40:42,006 --> 00:40:42,924
Fier!

642
00:40:42,949 --> 00:40:45,410
Fier, wait! Wait!

643
00:40:46,077 --> 00:40:47,078
- Fier!
- Ouch!

644
00:40:47,078 --> 00:40:47,704
Oh my god!

645
00:40:47,704 --> 00:40:49,372
Fier! Are you okay?

646
00:40:49,372 --> 00:40:50,540
Ouch!

647
00:40:50,540 --> 00:40:52,667
Fier, oh my god!
What's happening?

648
00:40:52,667 --> 00:40:54,836
Shut up, Alys! Ouch!

649
00:40:54,836 --> 00:40:56,463
Do you want me to call a doctor?

650
00:40:56,463 --> 00:40:57,672
Fier, please let me help you.

651
00:40:57,672 --> 00:40:59,257
Don't touch me, Alys!

652
00:40:59,809 --> 00:41:00,938
- Fier...
- Ouch!

653
00:41:42,383 --> 00:41:43,460
I'm right.

654
00:41:44,002 --> 00:41:45,545
This is gonna happen.

655
00:41:46,186 --> 00:41:48,814
I really want to be a responsible
husband to Alys.

656
00:41:49,673 --> 00:41:51,884
But I have to be a responsible father.

657
00:41:55,023 --> 00:41:56,608
But with all of this,

658
00:41:57,087 --> 00:41:59,297
all I'm thinking about is Alys.

659
00:41:59,609 --> 00:42:00,985
Only Alys.

660
00:42:02,195 --> 00:42:03,696
She's my world.

661
00:42:03,934 --> 00:42:05,352
She's my home.

662
00:42:06,282 --> 00:42:07,700
Only her.

663
00:42:08,868 --> 00:42:10,662
And I know through all of this,

664
00:42:11,454 --> 00:42:13,248
she'll have to bear my burdens.

665
00:42:14,666 --> 00:42:15,833
Alys,

666
00:42:16,918 --> 00:42:18,545
please be strong for me.

667
00:42:20,144 --> 00:42:21,104
For us.

668
00:42:23,434 --> 00:42:24,769
Fier is here.

669
00:42:26,238 --> 00:42:27,990
I hope we face this together.

670
00:42:30,348 --> 00:42:31,349
Please.

671
00:42:32,225 --> 00:42:33,226
Please.

672
00:42:33,726 --> 00:42:35,228
Please don't leave me.

673
00:42:36,570 --> 00:42:38,439
Or else I'll break.

674
00:42:39,322 --> 00:42:40,865
I need you, Alys.

675
00:42:41,142 --> 00:42:42,685
I need you, my noob.

676
00:43:14,767 --> 00:43:18,146
On the next episode of
Dating Alys Perez.

677
00:43:19,647 --> 00:43:22,066
You can't let her be angry at Alys.

678
00:43:22,567 --> 00:43:24,694
It's not good for the child.

679
00:43:24,902 --> 00:43:26,654
Drake, my decision is final.

680
00:43:27,363 --> 00:43:28,832
I'm leaving for now.

681
00:43:31,080 --> 00:43:32,623
- Shaira!
- Alys!

682
00:43:32,663 --> 00:43:34,721
You poor thing!

683
00:43:34,746 --> 00:43:36,539
I'm just accommodating Fier's needs.

684
00:43:36,757 --> 00:43:40,136
Because I'm pretty sure what
he's going through is not easy.

685
00:43:40,456 --> 00:43:42,792
But what you're going
through is not easy too, Alys!

686
00:43:43,310 --> 00:43:44,645
OMG!

687
00:43:44,670 --> 00:43:47,422
I knew you were stupid,
but not to this extent!

688
00:43:47,544 --> 00:43:49,296
- That's harsh.
- My god, please!

689
00:43:49,630 --> 00:43:50,425
Tripp,

690
00:43:51,110 --> 00:43:52,089
thank you.

691
00:43:52,388 --> 00:43:54,057
You didn't leave me.

692
00:43:54,265 --> 00:43:55,224
Not yet.

693
00:43:55,892 --> 00:43:57,101
I still can't.

694
00:43:57,894 --> 00:43:58,910
What?

695
00:43:59,020 --> 00:43:59,729
What?

696
00:43:59,729 --> 00:44:00,355
Nothing.

697
00:44:00,688 --> 00:44:04,901
I haven't a clue as to why
you're tolerating this bullshit!

698
00:44:05,041 --> 00:44:06,626
Alys, wake up!

699
00:44:06,758 --> 00:44:08,343
You're the wife!

700
00:44:08,576 --> 00:44:10,369
Why did you have to leave?

701
00:44:10,740 --> 00:44:11,777
Fuck it.

702
00:44:11,816 --> 00:44:14,319
Hey I'm not done with
you yet, Ms. Homewrecker!

703
00:44:14,939 --> 00:44:16,232
Miss Whoever-You-Are!

704
00:44:16,499 --> 00:44:18,042
Watch your fucking words!

705
00:44:18,414 --> 00:44:21,542
If Alys won't do anything about it,
I sure as hell will!
